#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:2
msgid "Main content detection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:4
msgid ""
"Read the Docs detects the main content area of HTML pages to focus on the"
" documentation content itself, ignoring headers, footers, navigation, and"
" other page elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:9
msgid "Feature usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:11
msgid "Different features use this detection in different ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:13
msgid ""
":doc:`/visual-diff`: Uses a documentation-tool specific heuristic first. "
"If you configure a custom selector it overrides that heuristic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:14
msgid ""
":doc:`/link-previews`: Uses the custom selector (if set) to scope links; "
"otherwise falls back to heuristics here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:15
msgid ""
":doc:`/server-side-search/index`: Always uses heuristics; it ignores any "
"configured custom selector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:18
msgid "Detection logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:20
msgid ""
"The main content node is detected using the following logic, in order of "
"priority:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:22
msgid ""
"**Elements with** ``role=\"main\"`` **attribute**: This ARIA role is used"
" by many static site generators and themes to indicate the main content "
"area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:23
msgid ""
"**The** ``<main>`` **HTML tag**: The semantic HTML5 element for main "
"content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:24
msgid ""
"**Parent of the first** ``<h1>`` **tag**: If no explicit main content "
"markers are found, the system assumes all sections are siblings under a "
"common parent, and uses the parent of the first heading as the main "
"content container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:25
msgid ""
"**The** ``<body>`` **tag**: As a last resort, if none of the above are "
"found, the entire body is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/reference/main-content-detection.rst:29
msgid ""
"Following the ARIA_ conventions will also improve the accessibility of "
"your site. See also https://webaim.org/techniques/semanticstructure/."
msgstr ""

